    <!-- Connection Guide Dialog Strings -->
    <string name="guide_dialog_title">📖 Universal Connection Guide (CarPlay &amp; Android Auto)</string>
    <string name="guide_dialog_subtitle">Step-by-step instructions for Apple iOS and Android devices</string>
    <string name="guide_ios_title">🍏 1. Apple iPhone (Apple CarPlay)</string>
    <string name="guide_ios_body">🔌 Direct USB Cable Connection:\n1. Connect iPhone directly to vehicle USB port or adapter using a quality data cable.\n2. Tap \'Trust This Computer\' or \'Allow CarPlay\' on your iPhone.\n3. CarTwin immediately starts Apple CarPlay video and audio.\n\n📡 Wireless Connection (Cable-free):\n1. Enable Bluetooth and Wi-Fi on iPhone.\n2. Pair with \'CarTwin\' from Bluetooth settings.\n3. Tap \'Use Wireless CarPlay\' on your phone.\n\n💡 Note: Siri must be enabled in iPhone Settings ➔ Siri &amp; Search.</string>
    <string name="guide_android_title">🤖 2. Android Phone (Samsung, Xiaomi, Pixel, Honor, etc.)</string>
    <string name="guide_android_body">🔌 Direct USB Cable Connection (AOA 2.0):\n1. Connect phone directly to vehicle USB port with a quality data cable.\n2. In the phone USB notification, select \'Android Auto / File Transfer\'.\n3. CarTwin identifies your phone model (Samsung, Xiaomi, Pixel, etc.) via AOA 2.0 and launches Android Auto.\n\n📡 Wireless Connection (Cable-free):\n1. Turn on Bluetooth and Wi-Fi on your phone.\n2. Pair with \'CarTwin\' in Bluetooth settings.\n3. Confirm \'Allow Wireless Android Auto\'.\n\n🎙️ Aura AI Assistant: Works for hands-free vehicle climate, navigation, and music control.</string>
    <string name="guide_faq_title">🛠️ 3. Troubleshooting &amp; FAQ</string>
    <string name="guide_faq_body">⚠️ Cable plugged in but no reaction?\n• Ensure the cable is a data cable (not charge-only) and \'Android Auto / File Transfer\' is selected.\n• If vehicle screen prompts for USB permission, select \'Always Allow\'.\n\n🔄 Connection dropped?\n• Tap \'Restart Services\' button on the screen.\n\n🎙️ How does Aura AI work?\n• Press steering wheel voice button or tap brand logo to speak in English, Azerbaijani, Turkish, or Russian.</string>

